 - Resume point is intact and mutually consistent: `history.json` has 20 completed entries (last `gen=19`, SHA-256 `2ad163e4a0af5ea9d4fb2584d116c58af60b0b1fa7ea966e92e7c3017416e1b0`); `cma.pkl` has `countiter=20`, σ `0.015219975232099293` (SHA-256 `4f8fb07f67ef13d7c54b65616e4dfbe3e466db4ceac8ee9a767ce419427502d3`). `gen_020/` was created but has **0 game rows** and is an unevaluated interruption artifact; it must not be interpreted as fitness evidence. The normal config/hash checks make restarting the existing CMA command resume safely at gen 20.
 - All 18 CMA4 workers are released. The predeclared fresh full-panel gate at `runs/t025_cma4_g005_and_g015_fresh_full_gate/arena/` remains its original, valid `--workers 4` invocation (516/960 rows at pause check); it was not resized mid-run, so its sample/pairing specification is unchanged. No Kaggle submission or candidate change occurred.
+
+## CMA4 resumed-gate control update and schedule (declared 2026-09-26, Codex before resume)
+
+- Claude independently confirmed and promoted `candidates/es6_c4g15/pkg/main.py`.  Starting with the next due CMA4 centre gate (completed **gen 20**) and every completed generation divisible by five thereafter, the frozen gate **CONTROL** is `candidates/es6_c4g15/pkg/main.py`, SHA-256 `53c93a2b3abc9997577ed53fa6ec9cae86f17303c88d670de6fa14561c2fc03a`.  `es5_c3g15` results remain historical and are not pooled with these tests.
