diff --git a//workspace/shared/tasks/T025-route-conditioned-land.md b//workspace/shared/tasks/T025-route-conditioned-land.md
index 77ff4ae0fac1a39a3dc37118e4d8c748b773d142..546d985e6531382d9b775e26f16f58a3797ee177
--- a//workspace/shared/tasks/T025-route-conditioned-land.md
+++ b//workspace/shared/tasks/T025-route-conditioned-land.md
@@ -177,3 +177,9 @@
 - At Claude's request, the local CMA4 search was allowed to finish its already-running gen 19, then its entire process group was terminated before it could evaluate gen 20. Gen 19 is complete: **1,056/1,056 games, zero errors**, centre fitness **1.0301984375**, best `x9` **1.0312548828125**, post-tell σ **0.015219975232099293**. This follows the declining g14→g18 centre sequence but does not itself make a candidate claim.
 - Resume point is intact and mutually consistent: `history.json` has 20 completed entries (last `gen=19`, SHA-256 `2ad163e4a0af5ea9d4fb2584d116c58af60b0b1fa7ea966e92e7c3017416e1b0`); `cma.pkl` has `countiter=20`, σ `0.015219975232099293` (SHA-256 `4f8fb07f67ef13d7c54b65616e4dfbe3e466db4ceac8ee9a767ce419427502d3`). `gen_020/` was created but has **0 game rows** and is an unevaluated interruption artifact; it must not be interpreted as fitness evidence. The normal config/hash checks make restarting the existing CMA command resume safely at gen 20.
 - All 18 CMA4 workers are released. The predeclared fresh full-panel gate at `runs/t025_cma4_g005_and_g015_fresh_full_gate/arena/` remains its original, valid `--workers 4` invocation (516/960 rows at pause check); it was not resized mid-run, so its sample/pairing specification is unchanged. No Kaggle submission or candidate change occurred.
+
+## CMA4 resumed-gate control update and schedule (declared 2026-09-26, Codex before resume)
+
+- Claude independently confirmed and promoted `candidates/es6_c4g15/pkg/main.py`.  Starting with the next due CMA4 centre gate (completed **gen 20**) and every completed generation divisible by five thereafter, the frozen gate **CONTROL** is `candidates/es6_c4g15/pkg/main.py`, SHA-256 `53c93a2b3abc9997577ed53fa6ec9cae86f17303c88d670de6fa14561c2fc03a`.  `es5_c3g15` results remain historical and are not pooled with these tests.
+- CMA4 training resumes from its untouched gen-19 `history.json`/`cma.pkl`, with the recorded `panel_rotating_8` fitness schedule and its recorded `es5_c3g15` training mirror unchanged.  Only the independent gate control changes.  The resumed trainer is capped at **14 workers**.
+- Each due gate freezes `runs/cma4/gen_NNN/c/main.py`, hashes it and the CONTROL before/after, draws 16 CSPRNG worlds excluded from every recoverable `runs/` seed artifact, and evaluates both agents in one `compare.py` run versus the same ten named strata, both seats (640 games; no implicit baselines).  It uses at most four workers.  The statistic and pass criteria are the existing fresh full-panel rule: nine equal-weight strata (eight core plus `es1_g9`/`v5_market` family), joint 16-world 200,000-resample one-sided paired-score lower bound strictly >0, and no named opponent point estimate below −10pp; all rows must be valid/DONE.  A pass makes a WIP evidence freeze only and is reported to Claude for independent review; it never submits to Kaggle.
diff --git a/lab/tools/t025_periodic_full_panel_gate.py b/lab/tools/t025_periodic_full_panel_gate.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..64977196ad8c6659268d469003cfff981dd10e39
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lab/tools/t025_periodic_full_panel_gate.py
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Run one declared T025 CMA4 full-panel gate against the current control.
+
+The invocation is intentionally one generation at a time.  It refuses reused
+output paths and recovers every prior recorded seed before drawing its panel.
+This makes the companion resume loop safe to leave running between gates.
+"""
+import argparse
+import hashlib
+import json
+import secrets
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+from pathlib import Path
+
+ROOT = Path("/workspace/wt/codex")
+SHARED = Path("/workspace/shared")
+RUNS = SHARED / "runs"
+CONTROL = SHARED / "candidates/es6_c4g15/pkg/main.py"
+OPPONENTS = {
+    "mirror": CONTROL,
+    "parthenos": SHARED / "opponents/pool/parthenos_robust/main.py",
+    "metav4": SHARED / "opponents/pool/tschinkel_metav4_v13/main.py",
+    "yhay0913": SHARED / "opponents/pool/yhay_router0913/main.py",
+    "t2945": SHARED / "opponents/pool/tschinkel2945/main.py",
+    "ozer_v45": SHARED / "opponents/pool/ozer_v45/main.py",
+    "yaxon": SHARED / "opponents/pool/yaxon_reactive_v5/main.py",
+    "pilkwang": SHARED / "opponents/pool/pilkwang_struct/main.py",
+    "es1_g9": SHARED / "candidates/es1_g9/pkg/main.py",
+    "v5_market": ROOT / "agents/horizon_v5_market.py",
+}
+
+
+def sha(path):
+    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
+
+
+def values(node):
+    if isinstance(node, dict):
+        out = set()
+        for key, value in node.items():
+            if key == "seed" and type(value) is int and 0 <= value < 2**31:
+                out.add(value)
+            elif key == "seeds" and isinstance(value, list):
+                out.update(v for v in value if type(v) is int and 0 <= v < 2**31)
+            else:
+                out |= values(value)
+        return out
